From: Ziyang Huang <hzyitc@outlook.com>

QCA8K can use ports 0 and 6 as CPU ports, but the setup path
selects only one of them. This leaves the hardware topology out of
sync with the per-user-port CPU assignment already made by DSA.

Remove the separate CPU-port selection and validate that every CPU
port is supported by the hardware. For each user port, program only
its assigned CPU port into lookup membership and add the reciprocal
membership on that CPU port.

Together with flooding unknown traffic to every CPU port, ingress
lookup membership limits delivery to the correct conduit and avoids
duplicate frames.

